{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nFive items in the plan-review attestation stack were independently confirmed dead, duplicated, or misdeclared (operator ruling: the residue is approved only because it was confirmed dead by both semantic references and string grep). Every `path:line` below was re-measured on origin/main `38f8587f65d`.\n\n**1 — a dead keyword-only parameter.** `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py:289 _hash_basis(repo_root=None, *, at_current_gate_ref: bool = False)`: every src caller passes no kwarg (`llm/code_review/region_gate.py:62`, `llm/code_review/sidecar.py:258`, `llm/plan_review/attest.py:226`, `llm/plan_review/manifest.py:440`, `llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py:193`). The branch at `:302-303` delegates to `gate_ref_hash_basis` (`manifest.py:240`), which is independently reachable and stays. Only `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ref_coherence.py:171,176,181,218` pass the kwarg. `docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md:119` records the consolidated boundary with the kwarg in its signature.\n\n**2 — a function with no consumer.** `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/read_set.py:189-214 terraform_membership_entries`, plus its doc-comment and constant at `:185-186 _TERRAFORM_GLOB_SUFFIXES`, has no src caller; only `tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py:223-231` exercises it. ADR 0115 `:86-87` defers remote module *content* only, not membership globs, so nothing is waiting on it; under ADR 0111 code waiting for a consumer is deleted.\n\n**3 — an enum member with no behaviour.** `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pin_health.py:15 PlanValidityProfile{DEFAULT,CLOSE,DRIFT_REFRESH}` is read in exactly one place, `attest.py:665 if profile is PlanValidityProfile.DEFAULT`. `CLOSE` and `DRIFT_REFRESH` (`pin_health.py:18`) are therefore behaviourally identical, and nothing serialises `.value` or `.name`. `tests/unit/test_attestation_invalidation.py:262-291` exists solely to assert that equivalence.\n\n**4 — a duplicated message.** `attest.py:426` and `attest.py:466` render a byte-identical \"… could not be resolved to a snapshot, so the attestation cannot …\" string from two arms.\n\n**5 — the status enum is misaligned with the wire in BOTH directions.** `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json:11`:\n\n- It **declares a value this surface cannot emit**: `not-closed` is produced only under `kind == \"completion-verifier\"` (`attest.py:622-628`). `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py:54` already asserts its exclusion from the plan-review vocabulary, documenting it at `:23` as \"reachable only inside the completion-verifier arm (attest.py), never for plan-review\".\n- It **omits a value this surface does emit**: `attest_gate.py:159` passes `signing.verify_signature`'s verdict through verbatim. Six of the seven failure verdicts are already declared, and deliberately — the enum's own description names `mismatch`, `invalid`, `foreign_key`, `unavailable`, `unknown_kind`, `unknown_scheme` as \"the signature-check verdicts a non-certified attestation can carry\". The seventh, `key_not_valid_at_era` (`src/rebar/types.py:379-389`; produced at `src/rebar/attest/opcert.py:308,330`), is **not** declared. It is the one genuine wire-vs-schema leak, and `tests/unit/test_opcert_cross_environment_c21f.py:225` observes it.\n\nThe pass-through is the contract rather than an accident, so the fix declares the missing member instead of suppressing the class: `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py:63` asserts the signature verdicts stay OUT of the blocking bucket and `:65` that `bucket_for_verdict(\"mismatch\") == \"infra\"` — a downstream consumer that already receives them and fails open.\n\nNeither `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py` nor `src/rebar/types.py` declares a `PlanReviewStatus` mirror (grep for both names over those files returns nothing), so the JSON Schema is the sole enum declaration and no other typed surface changes.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **`manifest.py`** — delete the `:302-303` branch and the `at_current_gate_ref` text in the `_hash_basis` docstring (`:294` and the bullet documenting the mode); the signature becomes `def _hash_basis(repo_root=None) -> str`. Remove the kwarg's name from `gate_ref_hash_basis`'s docstring at `:244`, which currently reads \"`_hash_basis` delegates here for its `at_current_gate_ref` mode\".\n2. **`read_set.py`** — delete `:185-186` (the `#:` comment and `_TERRAFORM_GLOB_SUFFIXES`) and `:189-214` (`terraform_membership_entries`).\n3. **`pin_health.py`** — delete `DRIFT_REFRESH` (`:18`). `attest.py:244` becomes `profile=PlanValidityProfile.CLOSE` with the comment \"CLOSE = skip code-freshness (the only non-DEFAULT behaviour)\". Reword the `attest.py:534` comment that names `DEFAULT/DRIFT_REFRESH`. `src/rebar/_commands/gates.py:229`, `attest_gate.py:172`, `src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py:232`, and `docs/plan-review-gate.md:1099` all name `DEFAULT` or `CLOSE` and are unchanged. The function `attest.drift_refresh_candidate` keeps its name — only the enum member it passes changes.\n4. **`attest.py`** — add `def _unresolvable_ref_reason(ref: str | None) -> str` returning the shared string (`named = f\"'{ref}'\" if ref else \"the configured gate ref\"`); the `:426` and `:466` arms each become a `return _unresolvable_ref_reason(...)` call.\n5. **Align the enum with the wire, leaving the `attest_gate.py:159` pass-through UNCHANGED.** In `plan_review_status.schema.json:11`, remove `not-closed` from the `enum` array and add `key_not_valid_at_era`; update the description sentence \"The last 6 values (…)\" so it names all 7 signature verdicts. Mirror both edits in the prose that restates the same vocabulary: `attest_gate.py:203` (drop `not-closed`) and `:208` (add `key_not_valid_at_era`); `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py:37` (drop `not-closed`) and `:40` (add `key_not_valid_at_era`). `src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py:379` is the completion-verifier surface where `not-closed` IS reachable — leave it.\n6. **`docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md:119`** — amend the recorded signature to `_hash_basis(repo_root)` and append an amendment note in the file's existing \"*(amended by …)*\" style, naming this story and pointing the gate-ref mode at `gate_ref_hash_basis`. The amended line must not retain the removed kwarg's name, because AC1 greps `docs`.\n7. **`docs/release-notes.md`** — add: \"`plan_review_status.verdict` enum realigned with what the surface actually emits: `not-closed` removed (reachable only in the completion-verifier arm, never for plan-review), and `key_not_valid_at_era` added (the signing verdict `attest_gate` has always passed through but the schema never declared). Backward-compatible for readers under `docs/api-stability.md:23`: no required key is removed or retyped, and the emitted set is now a subset of the declared enum.\"\n\n## Scope\n\nThe files named above. **Out of scope:** `_legacy_material_ok` (`attest.py:727`, callers `:71,634,687`, corpus contract `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py:10,39`); the delta explainers; `compute_validity`'s completion-verifier arm. `tests/fixtures/cloud_adf_corpus/bodies_00.json` and `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/code_arrow.json` each quote `at_current_gate_ref` inside a frozen archived report body — immutable corpus data, which is why AC1 carries the `':!tests/fixtures'` pathspec exclusion rather than silently failing against them.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ref_coherence.py:171,176,181,218` — `attest._hash_basis(str(repo), at_current_gate_ref=True)` becomes `manifest.gate_ref_hash_basis(str(repo)).path`; the assertions themselves are unchanged. The comments at `:167,174,178` that name the kwarg must also be reworded, since AC1 greps `tests`.\n- Delete `tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py:223-231` (`test_terraform_membership_entries_are_glob_dep_entries`).\n- `tests/unit/test_attestation_invalidation.py:262-291` — this test's only purpose is proving `CLOSE` and `DRIFT_REFRESH` agree (`assert close[\"valid\"] is refresh[\"valid\"] is True; assert close[\"health\"] == refresh[\"health\"]`). Mechanically rewriting `.DRIFT_REFRESH` to `.CLOSE` would leave it comparing a value to itself. **Delete the `refresh` block and both equivalence assertions**, keeping the `default`/`close` arms and asserting `default[\"verdict\"] == \"stale-head\"` and `close[\"valid\"] is True` — the profile distinction that survives.\n- `.DRIFT_REFRESH` becomes `.CLOSE` at `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_validity.py:35`, `tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_health_heldout.py:106`, and `tests/unit/test_drift_refresh_candidate.py:56`.\n- Add `tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_drift.py::test_unresolvable_ref_reason_is_single_sourced`: the scoped and unscoped paths both yield `_unresolvable_ref_reason(ref)` verbatim.\n- Add to `tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py` a parametrized test over all 7 `verify_signature` failure verdicts asserting that each is passed through unchanged as `verdict` and that the result validates against `plan_review_status.schema.json` with `jsonschema` — the oracle for \"declared enum ⊇ emitted set\". Include a negative case asserting `not-closed` is rejected by the schema.\n- Unchanged: `tests/unit/test_opcert_cross_environment_c21f.py:225`, `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py` (whole file), `tests/unit/test_compute_validity.py:28`, `tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py:428` (both completion-arm).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `git grep -n \"at_current_gate_ref\\|terraform_membership_entries\\|DRIFT_REFRESH\\|_TERRAFORM_GLOB_SUFFIXES\" -- src tests docs ':!tests/fixtures'` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `git grep -c \"could not be resolved to a snapshot\" -- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py` prints `1`.\n- [ ] `python -c \"import json;e=json.load(open('src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json'))['properties']['verdict']['enum'];print('not-closed' in e, 'key_not_valid_at_era' in e)\"` prints `False True`.\n- [ ] `python -c \"import json;e=set(json.load(open('src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json'))['properties']['verdict']['enum']);print({'mismatch','invalid','foreign_key','unavailable','unknown_kind','unknown_scheme','key_not_valid_at_era'} <= e)\"` prints `True`.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py:159` still reads `\"verdict\": result.get(\"verdict\", \"unsigned\"),` — the pass-through is retained, not suppressed.\n- [ ] `grep -c \"not-closed\" src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py` prints `1` (the completion-verifier surface keeps it).\n- [ ] The new parametrized status test and `test_unresolvable_ref_reason_is_single_sourced` are green, and `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py` passes **unmodified**.\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types --check` is clean; `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793396316663550022,"uuid":"8963eb97-b8a8-41a4-a0c9-96398cec2379"}